<question type="description"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Section 7: The Story — Part 11</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Section 7: The Story — Part 11</h3>
<p><strong>The Healing</strong></p>
<p><em>Narrative note: The king, having fallen ill, begs for physical
and spiritual salvation. Notice the dense use of verbal suffixes (fast
direct objects) as he pleads with Yukhannan.</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 1</strong></p>
<p>ܘܒܝܘܡܐ ܗ̣ܘ ܢܦܠ ܡܠܟܐ ܒܟܘܪܗܢܐ ܒܝܫܐ w-b-yawmā haw npal malkā b-kurhānā
bīšā. w-b-yawmā (and-in-day) haw (that) npal (fell) malkā (the-king)
b-kurhānā (in-illness) bīšā (evil/bad). → And in that day, the king fell
into a severe illness.</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 2</strong></p>
<p>ܘܐܬܐ ܠܘܬ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܘܢܦܠ ܩܕܡܘܗܝ ܘܐܡܪ ܠܗ w-ʾetā l-wāt Yūḥannan, w-npal
qdāmāw-hy, w-ʾemar l-eh: w-ʾetā (and-came) l-wāt (to-the-presence-of)
Yūḥannan (John), w-npal (and-fell) qdāmāw-hy (before-him), w-ʾemar
(and-said) l-eh (to-him): → And he came to Yukhannan, and fell before
him, and said to him:</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 3</strong></p>
<p>ܐܣܐܝܢܝ ܡܢ ܟܘܪܗܢܝ ܘܦܪܘܩܝܢܝ ܡܢ ܡܘܬܐ ʾassaynī men kurhān-y, w-pruqaynī
men mawtā! ʾassaynī (heal-me [Paael Impv + 1csg]) men (from) kurhān-y
(illness-my), w-pruqaynī (and-save-me [Peal Impv + 1csg]) men (from)
mawtā (death)! → “Heal me from my illness, and save me from death!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 4</strong></p>
<p>ܘܫܒܘܩ ܠܝ ܚܛܝܬܝ ܕܣܓܝܐܐ ܗܝ w-šbūq lī ḥṭīt-y d-saggīʾā hī! w-šbūq
(and-forgive [Peal Impv]) lī (to-me) ḥṭīt-y (sin-my) d-saggīʾā
(which-is-great/much) hī (she-[is])! → “And forgive me my sin, which is
great!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 5</strong></p>
<p>ܩܪܐ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܠܐܠܗܐ ܘܐܡܪ qrā Yūḥannan l-ʾAlāhā w-ʾemar: qrā (called [3msg
Peal Perf. of q-r-y]) Yūḥannan (John) l-ʾAlāhā (upon-God) w-ʾemar
(and-said): → Yukhannan called upon God and said: <em>Note: When a
III-Yodh 3 m.sg. perfect verb takes a 3 m.sg. object suffix (“he called
him”), it attaches <code>-yhy</code> after the final <code>-ā</code>
vowel: qrā + -yhy → ܩܪܝܗܝ (qrāyhy), whereas 3 m.pl. qrāw + -hy → qrāwhy
(“they called him”).</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 6</strong></p>
<p>ܐܠܗܐ ܢܢܝܚܟ ܘܢܚܝܟ ܗܫܐ ʾAlāhā nnīḥ-āḵ, w-naḥē-ḵ hāšā. ʾAlāhā (God)
nnīḥ-āḵ (he-will-give-rest-to-you [Aphel Imperfect of n-w-ḥ]), w-naḥē-ḵ
(and-he-will-give-life/save-you [Aphel Imperfect of ḥ-y-y]) hāšā (now).
→ “God will give you rest, and will save you now.”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 7</strong></p>
<p>ܘܫܡܥܗ ܐܠܗܐ ܒܛܝܒܘܬܗ ܘܫܪܝ ܠܡܐܣܝܘܬܗ w-šamʿ-eh ʾAlāhā b-ṭaybūt-eh,
w-šarrī l-mʾassyūt-eh. w-šamʿ-eh (and-heard-him) ʾAlāhā (God)
b-ṭaybūt-eh (by-grace-his), w-šarrī (and-began) l-mʾassyūt-eh
(to-heal-him). → And God heard him by his grace, and began to heal
him.</p>
<hr />

]]></text></questiontext></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 9</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[In the story, what three commands does the sick king give Yukhannan?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Heal me, save me, forgive me (<i>ʾassaynī, pruqaynī, šbūq lī</i>)]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct (sentences 3–4).]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Leave my land, fear me, worship me]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in this part.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Pray for me, bless me, baptize me]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Kill my enemies, save my kingdom, heal my son]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 10</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Why does the king ask for forgiveness?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Because his sin is great (<i>saggīʾā hī</i>)]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Because he is about to die]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[He asks to be saved from death, but the forgiveness is for his great sin.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Because Yukhannan demanded it]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Because the people rebelled]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 11</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Who performs the healing in sentence 7?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[God, by his grace]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct: <i>šamʿeh ʾAlāhā b-ṭaybūteh, w-šarrī l-mʾassyūteh</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Yukhannan, by his own power]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[He prayed; God healed.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The king's physicians]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not in the story.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[The man of fire]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That was in Lesson 10.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 12</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 1. Identify ܩܛܠ ܐܢܘܢ (<i>qṭal ʾennōn</i>).]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root q-ṭ-l + 3 m.pl. enclitic object <i>ʾennōn</i>: 'he killed them']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root q-ṭ-l, subject 3 m.pl.: 'they killed']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That is <i>qṭalū</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root q-ṭ-l, suffix 2 m.pl.: 'he killed you (pl.)']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That suffix is -ḵūn.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root q-ṭ-l-h]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>ʾennōn</i> is the 3 m.pl. enclitic object pronoun.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 13</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 1. Identify ܦܪܩܢܝ (<i>parqanī</i>).]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root p-r-q, suffix 1 c.sg.: 'he delivered me']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root p-r-q, suffix 1 c.pl.: 'us']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA['Us' is -an.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root p-r-q-n]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[-anī is a suffix with the n buffer.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Root p-r-q, 'my redemption']]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That noun is <i>purqān-y</i>.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 14</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 1. What is the root of ܩܪܝܗܝ (<i>qrāyhy</i>), 'he called him'?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[q-r-y, a III-Yodh root]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct: the final yodh combines with the suffix -hy.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[q-r-w]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not this root.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[q-r-b]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[That is 'draw near'.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[r-y-h]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Not this.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
<question type="multichoice"><name><text>Module 3 · Lesson 11 · Check 15</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[Exercise 2. Attach suffixes to <i>šbaq</i>: which list means 'he abandoned me, us, her, them (m.)'?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></generalfeedback><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>šabqanī, šabqan, šabqāh, šbaq ʾennōn</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>šabqan, šabqanī, šabqāh, šbaq ʾennōn</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[-anī is 'me'; -an is 'us'.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>šabqanī, šabqan, šabqeh, šbaq ʾennōn</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[-eh is 'him'; 'her' is -āh.]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<i>šbaqt, šbaqn, šebqat, šbaqū</i>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Those are subject endings, not object suffixes.]]></text></feedback></answer></question>
